Xray-core: leave a failing door only for a calmer one, on the same server when possible

Two changes to the failover of the autoselect outbound (xray-autoselect.patch).

1. A suspect selection is left only for a member that has not failed for a
   minute, or whose share of failed recent connections is lower by at least
   0.25. A dead selection still moves at once, to any working member.
   Without this a phone could move back and forth many times an hour
   between two Cloudflare doors that both mostly worked, and each of those
   moves changed the server its traffic left from.

2. A new "exits" setting names the server each member sends traffic out
   from. A failover prefers a member with the exit of the one it leaves,
   unless another member is faster by the margin that replaces a healthy
   selection (switchRatio and switchMinGain together). Without this,
   failovers left one server's direct door for another server's Cloudflare
   door while the first server's own Cloudflare door was in the same group.

